{
  "committed_or_pushed": false,
  "decisions": [
    "Control learning reuses the exact original acquisition/forgetting row-index sequence. Code rotation changes only old code/target fields; no rebalancing. Old/new input UID and token schedule hashes asserted.",
    "alternate_binding uses old128 then new128 with continuous AdamW; new_only uses new128 from identical initial adapter and fresh AdamW. Midpoint observations do not reset optimizer.",
    "Own alternate acquisition requires accuracy>=.8 and gain>=.3, at least6 old intents; same new-skill gate at least6. Stop alternate before new training if old acquisition fails.",
    "Shared sample is historical eligible intersect alternate own acquired; require4 per source,8 per split,two sources per split and all8 control source gates. No original-code control baseline filter or control forgetting criterion.",
    "All repairs target original codes with unchanged accuracy/gain/new-guard qualification. Each 2/4/8/16 arm has a fresh optimizer and exact original support prefixes. Budgets never selected by control outcomes.",
    "Completed historical grids are verified before control repairs. TEST additionally requires completed original forecast with matching hashes and chronological ordering.",
    "Paired curves include baseline0, raw guard excess, relative guard damage, utility and qualification. Minimum budget may be never; later qualification loss retained. Report per source plus equal-source means, with pooled intents descriptive only.",
    "Controls do not enter any original predictor fit, lens calibration, feature selection or forecast. Original frozen prediction pipeline unchanged."
  ],
